Description: CVE-2026-63383 - Fix out-of-bounds read in decode_tag_internal
 libevent before 2.1.13 and 2.2.2-alpha has an out-of-bounds read in
 decode_tag_internal() in event_tagging.c. The function requests a limited
 number of bytes via evbuffer_pullup() (at most sizeof(number) + 1) but then
 iterates the decode loop using the full logical buffer length (len). A
 fragmented evbuffer containing a malformed multi-byte tag can therefore cause
 the loop to dereference bytes past the region actually made contiguous by
 evbuffer_pullup(), leading to an out-of-bounds read that can crash a process
 handling attacker-controlled RPC (evrpc) data.
 .
 This backports the upstream fix, which stores the pull-up length in a local
 variable (pullup_len) and bounds both the evbuffer_pullup() request and the
 decode loop on that same value, so the loop never reads beyond the pulled-up
 region.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/91ed8745eebabdd27592a83d350338a8c4626321
